WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.155
What a working engineer does on day one.

2
00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.141
Inventory before you build.

3
00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:13.509
List the document types and their counts, open ten of each, and note which ones are scanned, which have tables that matter, and which systems hold their permissions.

4
00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:17.907
Route each type to the cheapest parser that passes a small measured sample.

5
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:27.467
Add the silent-failure checks before the first full run, attach the metadata record, deduplicate with a written policy, and keep offsets back into the source.

6
00:00:27.747 --> 00:00:31.267
Then, and only then, start chunking, which is the next lesson.
